    "title": "Two threads share one counter (non-atomic increment)",
    "language": "WML/1",
    "source": "model counter_race \"Two threads share one counter (non-atomic increment)\"\ndescription \"Each thread reads the shared counter into a private register, then writes register + 1 back. The read and the write are separate atomic steps, so the scheduler may interleave them.\"\n\nvar counter : 0..2 = 0\n\nprocess A, B {\n  var pc  : {start, read_done, done} = start\n  var tmp : 0..2 = 0\n\n  // step 1: load the shared value into a private register\n  action read when pc = start {\n    tmp := counter\n    pc  := read_done\n  }\n\n  // step 2: store register + 1 (the check-then-act window is between read and write)\n  action write when pc = read_done {\n    counter := tmp + 1\n    pc      := done\n  }\n}\n\nterminal A.pc = done and B.pc = done\n\ninvariant NoLostUpdate: (A.pc = done and B.pc = done) => counter = 2\n",
    "sourceSha256": "4cce14cc874d6222af9a7c29f182e0b16f1310772240085f9776b57db3e5a6de",
